193670 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193668 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193670 #edb/ref 1061 41924 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193670 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9d5d8127-b825-594a-81df-e04296e04e38" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193670 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192793 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193702 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193670 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193702 #edb/ref 1061 44507 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193702 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96d5ce65-6ad2-5f74-bcdb-8d90d0ff8464" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193702 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192808 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193891 #edb/ref 1064 "The **boundary** of a set $S,$ denoted $\\partial S,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $S.$\n\nFor example, consider the set $A,$ given by \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, -1 \\lt x \\leq 1, \\, 0 \\lt y \\leq 2 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent this set as the following shaded region.\n\n![](images/50/5033928a09f9c320973a223bfd49b4b67924b433c7ba53e58bc07a95905f4231.png)\n\nThen, the set $\\partial A,$ the boundary of $A,$ has the following representation in the plane.\n\n![](images/e2/e2034b17b6a6834c1d747e2eba4a2522c43e9ff888d5f7feb7bf716b3e2cec00.png)\n\nThe **interior** of a set $S,$ denoted $\\textrm{int}\\, S,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $S.$ It contains every point in $S$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,S = S - \\partial S\n$$\n\nFor our set $A$ defined above, the interior looks as follows:\n\n![](images/57/57ab8735d761926a36aa0e469b4637482c31880cc446d913f93755a12ec65a8f.png)\n\nMore formally, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{int}\\,A = \\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, -1 \\lt x \\lt 1, \\, 0 \\lt y \\lt 2 \\big\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193891 #edb/ref 1065 6925 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193891 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0e637424-4284-59d5-be69-a86587836ad8" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186193891 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186275704 #edb/ref 1081 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186275704 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186275704 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "1762dd7a-cdff-5568-977d-6d80f2adc2de" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276211 #edb/ref 1081 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276211 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276211 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "51545767-3cc2-5437-9f48-638348ea4cb8" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276397 #edb/ref 1081 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276397 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276397 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "65e476b0-8d46-5284-adff-7ab3dfc01d42" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276725 #edb/ref 1081 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276725 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276725 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "89802e03-4038-5079-a2d6-6fbcbfaa4f4f" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276734 #edb/ref 1081 "None of the statements are true" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276734 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276734 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "8a5f5c40-cedb-5337-a6d5-fdb5d40c8667" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276747 #edb/ref 1081 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276747 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276747 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "8b30765e-36b9-5ec6-98f6-842bac2a8047" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276981 #edb/ref 1081 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276981 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186276981 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "a64a6892-a119-5289-a94b-626583cc70ba" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277057 #edb/ref 1081 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277057 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277057 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "af9e721c-402a-5c3f-9692-3951b59def5a" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277546 #edb/ref 1081 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277546 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277546 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "ebbc21fd-75c6-57b1-b5df-f0a1cd6cf1c3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277692 #edb/ref 1081 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277692 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277692 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "fbea97be-23e3-55aa-9854-424f79b2abcb" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276211 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276397 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276734 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277546 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277692 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186276397 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186277946 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "79c6778a-20db-511f-af8b-42a6afc7a710" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275704 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276725 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276747 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276981 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277057 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186276725 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278047 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "b45260eb-ab24-5e89-9cc0-6905bd2dcc59" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278047 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278578 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161622" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278578 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278578 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -1+x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4104ec23-658c-58b7-8dbf-72086dab259b" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278578 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/3e/3e7d8c11ac4b3de8473741a362ad2b78555c764da2d61f955435e8d59771cf46.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278580 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277946 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278580 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161625" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278580 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278580 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 2-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278580 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be0484aa-ac87-5330-9ede-cd54e1386a15" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278580 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cdca164d343d8bff4c78a1e366e52c588ca6c54dfdea61acea1900bcbdc79f31.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statements I and II are false. As we have seen, $A$ contains all its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278772 #edb/ref 1081 "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278772 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278772 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "1325c53d-2a90-5778-afb8-06fcd3205174" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278800 #edb/ref 1081 "0\\le x<2,\\text{ }0\\le y<2" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278800 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186278800 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "16ed68dd-7aef-5656-ac3a-0cafe1572795" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186279094 #edb/ref 1081 "0\\le x\\le 2,\\text{ }0<y<2" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186279094 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186279094 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "38d4ea31-5c92-59e1-b1b8-86206c057d4a" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186279233 #edb/ref 1081 "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186279233 #edb