ddc72bb410b3136f546705676f83d23d9071ffe972c5163d11af549.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/75/75e0132cd3854f18e9ab409b7fd13af3898f78b5174647bf2b33b8438b9228cb.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281312 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281051 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281312 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161721" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281312 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281312 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6d/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281312 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eb88fa68-158a-5357-aaca-59045c1933c3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281312 #edb/ref 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0b805c707981b9b6fcfa2ed387ad32a024fc845e6fd355a4b751ede4ad6a97e.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/69/69708aa698c38f8a29d3eb69083f893fd8fca183bd713387456624fc38b86fe9.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407131 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref